  "walkthrough-note": "THE FIRST-CONTACT WALKTHROUGH'S MAP SITES (spoke W, ideas/plans/onboarding-walkthrough.md). Ids only, never prose and never coordinates, for the reason the reveal's beats carry ids only: a sidecar that spelled a label out would ship the previous wording the day a content pass renames it. \`unfold\` is the box the TOOL opens on beat 4 and \`edit\` is the STATEMENT the reader drags on beat 5, with the effect read at \`read\`; the climax site was signed off 2026-08-07 (a single statement edit, never an evidence and never multi-handle). \`through\` and \`steady\` are optional colour: the intermediate step the consequence travels through, and a node that visibly holds still. Re-measured 2026-08-07 at asi-soon=0.1: everyone-dies 0.759 -> 0.581, if-built 0.883 -> 0.664, asi-soon itself implies 0.348, shutdown 0.970 -> 0.971 (both render 97%, so the steady line says 'holds at 97%', never 'does not move'). A beat whose ids this map no longer has is SKIPPED, not fatal (tours/walkthrough.ts beatIsReachable).",
